WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.535
-Hello!
-Thank you, and welcome.

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:03.669
Look at you.

00:00:03.669 --> 00:00:05.104
You always have something.

00:00:05.104 --> 00:00:06.639
I want to thank you again
for being here,

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:08.308
'cause you were
here back in April.

00:00:08.308 --> 00:00:09.342
-Yeah.

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:12.212
-And so much has changed
since then.

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:15.915
Obviously, you're now back
filming season three of "Pose."

00:00:15.915 --> 00:00:18.083
-Yes.
-How is it going?

00:00:18.083 --> 00:00:20.119
-It's wild.
It's crazy.

00:00:20.119 --> 00:00:21.587
I'm excited to be back.

00:00:21.587 --> 00:00:23.656
We're all glad to be back.

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:31.064
Disney, who now owns FX, has put
brilliant protocols in place.

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:33.233
Everybody looks like
a stormtrooper.

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:36.935
-[ Laughs ]
-I feel so sorry for the crew,

00:00:36.935 --> 00:00:41.006
because they have to have
goggles and masks and shields.

00:00:41.006 --> 00:00:42.441
-They have that here, too,
I agree.

00:00:42.441 --> 00:00:45.879
-But that allows for us
to be able to go to work.

00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:47.613
This is a wild, crazy time.

00:00:47.613 --> 00:00:51.017
And I'm just grateful that there
are people

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:54.854
who care enough
to take the right steps,

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:57.457
to believe science
and get us back to work.

00:00:57.457 --> 00:01:00.492
-You were nominated
for another Emmy this year.

00:01:00.492 --> 00:01:02.228
And even though it was virtual,

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:05.798
you still showed up and
delivered with awesome style.

00:01:05.798 --> 00:01:07.734
Look at that, come on, now.
-Ah!

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:09.769
-Come on, now.
-Yes.

00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:14.040
-What is the piano?

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.642
-Okay, so, I'm working
with a new stylist,

00:01:16.642 --> 00:01:20.279
Ty Hunter of Beyoncé fame.

00:01:20.279 --> 00:01:27.020
And he and his assistant Colin
showed up on Emmy day

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:31.691
with a piano that they had found
the night before on Craigslist

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:33.493
and spray-painted white.
-I love it.

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:35.728
-And they brought a backdrop
and a photographer,

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:38.130
and they came out
to my front yard,

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:40.032
and we took some photos,
darling.

00:01:40.032 --> 00:01:41.367
-I love that you did that.

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:44.003
You know, I don't know
if anyone else did that

00:01:44.003 --> 00:01:45.405
for, like, a virtual event.

00:01:45.405 --> 00:01:47.106
So that was pretty cool
that you did that.

00:01:47.106 --> 00:01:48.307
-It was my first.

00:01:48.307 --> 00:01:51.043
It was my first,
because I hadn't been doing

00:01:51.043 --> 00:01:53.513
any virtual red carpets
through the entire quarantine.

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:56.348
And I just thought
this will pack a punch,

00:01:56.348 --> 00:01:57.984
because
I'm nominated for an Emmy.

00:01:57.984 --> 00:01:59.119
It's a big deal.

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:01.120
And I haven't been doing them.
-Yeah.

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:02.589
And I bet you everyone
has been calling

00:02:02.589 --> 00:02:04.023
and asking, "Will Billy show up?

00:02:04.023 --> 00:02:06.326
And will Billy
do something for us?

00:02:06.326 --> 00:02:09.161
Will he get the hat?
Will he do something?"

00:02:09.161 --> 00:02:10.396
And you go, "Yeah, just chill.

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:13.800
I'll take care of business."
-Yeah.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:18.871
I wasn't doing it
because the moment that we're in

00:02:18.871 --> 00:02:22.675
didn't make me feel like
doing anything like that.

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:23.976
-Yeah. I agree.

00:02:23.976 --> 00:02:26.945
-You know, and so I
just wanted to be respectful.

00:02:26.945 --> 00:02:29.515
-Yeah.
-And I think, you know,

00:02:29.515 --> 00:02:33.286
having six months
of not doing that, you know,

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:35.254
and then embracing it
for the moment,

00:02:35.254 --> 00:02:37.857
which was the Emmys,
was a good thing.

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:39.525
-And it made people happy.
-Yes.

00:02:39.525 --> 00:02:41.927
-And you see the things
that we miss, and you go,

00:02:41.927 --> 00:02:43.196
"Aw, I miss that."
-Yes.

00:02:43.196 --> 00:02:44.531
-Sadly, you know,
Broadway announced

00:02:44.531 --> 00:02:47.266
that it will be shut down
through June,

00:02:47.266 --> 00:02:48.433
which is just awful.

00:02:48.433 --> 00:02:49.835
You think about this.

00:02:49.835 --> 00:02:52.171
You've been doing a lot
to celebrate Broadway,

00:02:52.171 --> 00:02:54.273
as we wait for it to come back.

00:02:54.273 --> 00:02:59.245
One of your early Broadway roles
was Teen Angel in "Grease,"

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:01.046
and you posted a photo
of your first time

00:03:01.046 --> 00:03:02.514
on "The Tonight Show."

00:03:02.514 --> 00:03:04.450
Here it is.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:06.853
-What do you remember
about this?

00:03:06.853 --> 00:03:10.456
-I remember that we were on tour

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:13.793
with the pre-Broadway production
of "Grease,"

00:03:13.793 --> 00:03:16.429
that starred Rosie O'Donnell
and Megan Mullally.

00:03:16.429 --> 00:03:19.799
-Megan Mullally?
-Pre-"Will &amp; Grace."

00:03:19.799 --> 00:03:22.335
-I did not know that.
-And we were in Costa Mesa,

00:03:22.335 --> 00:03:25.304
and "The Tonight Show"
was going to have us,

00:03:25.304 --> 00:03:28.740
and they came to the show,
and they saw the whole show.

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:30.743
And they chose my number.

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:34.113
And so I ended up
being able to go on.

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:37.550
And then it was a surprise,
because after the number,

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:42.521
Jay Leno paneled me,
which was a big deal.

00:03:42.521 --> 00:03:45.591
Because, like, I wasn't supposed
to go and talk.

00:03:45.591 --> 00:03:47.893
I was just supposed to be
a musical guest and sing.

00:03:47.893 --> 00:03:50.797
-And you scored.
-Yes.

00:03:50.797 --> 00:03:55.534
-There's this trend online
right now, I just recently did,

00:03:55.534 --> 00:03:59.171
where people share photos
and they go how it started,

00:03:59.171 --> 00:04:00.539
and how it's going.

00:04:00.539 --> 00:04:02.642
And people are doing it.
You've been having fun with it.

00:04:02.642 --> 00:04:04.476
You made one
just for us tonight.

00:04:04.476 --> 00:04:05.912
-Yes.
-Let's take a look at this.

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:09.515
Now, that is how it started,
which I have questions about.

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:11.517
-[ Laughs ]
-I see how it's going.

00:04:11.517 --> 00:04:12.651
Let's start with how it's going.

00:04:12.651 --> 00:04:14.854
Where was that?
Was that "Kinky Boots"?

00:04:14.854 --> 00:04:17.757
-That was "Kinky Boots," 2013,
the Tony Awards.

00:04:17.757 --> 00:04:18.925
-Oh, come on.

00:04:18.925 --> 00:04:20.592
-So that was the original dream
come true.

00:04:20.592 --> 00:04:22.394
The dream that I started having

00:04:22.394 --> 00:04:24.630
when you see me
on the left over there.

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:26.966
-Now, what was happening when
you're on the left over there?

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:29.835
How old are you?
-Okay, so, I am 13 years old.

00:04:29.835 --> 00:04:31.537
I was at Reizenstein
Middle School.

00:04:31.537 --> 00:04:35.207
I had discovered musical theater
in the sixth grade.

00:04:35.207 --> 00:04:36.742
I was in the eighth grade.

00:04:36.742 --> 00:04:38.211
And I figured,

00:04:38.211 --> 00:04:41.880
here I've spent the last
two years playing second banana.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:44.684
So I'm going to be
the star of the show.

00:04:44.684 --> 00:04:46.885
The show was announced.
It's "Oliver."

00:04:46.885 --> 00:04:48.187
I went to the library.

00:04:48.187 --> 00:04:49.822
I took out the cast album.

00:04:49.822 --> 00:04:51.757
I learned "Where Is Love?"

00:04:51.757 --> 00:04:54.326
I came, I sang,
I did my audition.

00:04:54.326 --> 00:04:57.429
The cast list goes up,
and it says Oliver Twist --

00:04:57.429 --> 00:04:59.766
Eric Pearson.

00:04:59.766 --> 00:05:04.036
Well, I storm
into the director's office.

00:05:04.036 --> 00:05:05.037
Mr. Ken Lutz,

00:05:05.037 --> 00:05:06.506
who was the instrumental
teacher,

00:05:06.506 --> 00:05:08.540
who I'm still friends
with to this day.

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:10.075
And I was like, "How dare you?"

00:05:10.075 --> 00:05:11.344
You know, like,
I went off on him.

00:05:11.344 --> 00:05:14.847
And he said, "Billy, Billy,
Billy, you, Fagin."

00:05:14.847 --> 00:05:18.317
If anybody knows "Oliver Twist,"
I was cast as Fagin.

00:05:18.317 --> 00:05:19.985
Fagin is really the star
of the show.

00:05:19.985 --> 00:05:22.221
Fagin is really the lead.
And I was like, "Okay."

00:05:22.221 --> 00:05:24.122
He said, "Well, take the script
home and read it."

00:05:24.122 --> 00:05:27.326
Well, of course, at 13,
you're just counting your lines.

00:05:27.326 --> 00:05:29.395
And Fagin, I was just
counting my lines.

00:05:29.395 --> 00:05:31.263
And Fagin doesn't even enter

00:05:31.263 --> 00:05:34.634
until the last scene
of the first act.

00:05:34.634 --> 00:05:36.836
I was like, "How are you
going to tell me

00:05:36.836 --> 00:05:38.571
I'm the lead of a show
named 'Oliver'

00:05:38.571 --> 00:05:40.173
and I'm not playing Oliver?"

00:05:40.173 --> 00:05:42.274
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:42.274 --> 00:05:44.777
-But that is when I discovered

00:05:44.777 --> 00:05:48.614
the power
of a star entrance, darling.

00:05:48.614 --> 00:05:50.515
Because the children
were waiting for me!

00:05:50.515 --> 00:05:52.851
I didn't realize it was that.
-[ Laughing ] Oh, my God.

00:05:52.851 --> 00:05:54.520
-I didn't understand that.

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:56.855
-Oh, my gosh.
This is ridiculous.

00:05:56.855 --> 00:05:58.190
-The children were
waiting for me.

00:05:58.190 --> 00:06:02.127
At 13, I arrived on the stage
to applause, darling.

00:06:02.127 --> 00:06:03.930
-The children were
waiting for you.

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:05.230
Oh, my gosh.

00:06:05.230 --> 00:06:07.133
I don't think
there's anything more --

00:06:07.133 --> 00:06:10.002
you get that special feeling
when a kid is doing "Oliver,"

00:06:10.002 --> 00:06:11.871
and they sing
"Where Is Love?"

00:06:11.871 --> 00:06:14.673
Just, like, the voice,
and it's just so little.

00:06:14.673 --> 00:06:18.744
-Yeah, but for me,
I'm reviewing the situation,

00:06:18.744 --> 00:06:23.048
an octave up
in a Pittsburgh/cockney accent.

00:06:23.048 --> 00:06:25.417
There is video.
I don't know where it is.

00:06:25.417 --> 00:06:27.786
But I'm sure
somebody will post it now

00:06:27.786 --> 00:06:29.355
when they see this.

00:06:29.355 --> 00:06:30.790
-Next time you come on,
we got to play that.

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:33.626
-It's out there somewhere.
[ Laughs ]

00:06:33.626 --> 00:06:36.629
-Billy, you've also been using
your platform

00:06:36.629 --> 00:06:38.664
to encourage people to vote.

00:06:38.664 --> 00:06:39.665
-Yes.

00:06:39.665 --> 00:06:41.433
-Like your beautiful
blazer says.

00:06:41.433 --> 00:06:42.935
And be active.

00:06:42.935 --> 00:06:46.005
I know last time you were on,
we talked about your version of

00:06:46.005 --> 00:06:48.374
"For What It's Worth."
-Yes.

00:06:48.374 --> 00:06:51.143
-Man, oh, man, did it explode.
Everyone loved it.

00:06:51.143 --> 00:06:54.380
It ended up being on
Obama's summer playlist.

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:56.682
-Yes.

00:06:56.682 --> 00:06:59.952
-Did you freak out?
You go, "Wait. Wow."

00:06:59.952 --> 00:07:02.488
-It's just -- It's astonishing.

00:07:02.488 --> 00:07:06.191
I've been an independent artist
for a long time.

00:07:06.191 --> 00:07:10.495
I had a R&amp;B record deal
back in the late '90s,

00:07:10.495 --> 00:07:12.031
and they dismissed me.

00:07:12.031 --> 00:07:14.199
So I've been on my own.

00:07:14.199 --> 00:07:17.636
I've been doing
independent music for a while.

00:07:17.636 --> 00:07:23.308
So to have this happen,
to be able to crack through

00:07:23.308 --> 00:07:24.876
in this way for something

00:07:24.876 --> 00:07:30.015
that I just remained persistent
and consistent on

00:07:30.015 --> 00:07:31.784
is really, really amazing.

00:07:31.784 --> 00:07:36.389
It's really powerful, and, it's
made it to the list of,

00:07:36.389 --> 00:07:39.458
like, being in contention
for a Grammy.

00:07:39.458 --> 00:07:41.393
-[ Clapping ]
This is what I'm talking about.

00:07:41.393 --> 00:07:45.163
See, that's what you do.
-So I am like just keep going.

00:07:45.163 --> 00:07:47.699
If there's anything that
I can say to folks,

00:07:47.699 --> 00:07:50.636
just keep going, just keep
showing up for your life

00:07:50.636 --> 00:07:52.271
and putting one foot
in front of the other.

00:07:52.271 --> 00:07:53.706
-It was great.
I love that you did it.

00:07:53.706 --> 00:07:57.910
And I was so happy
to see it on that list.

00:07:57.910 --> 00:08:00.612
I go, "Oh, he's got to be, like,
just freaking out right now."

00:08:00.612 --> 00:08:02.914
-Yeah, it's amazing.
It's amazing.

00:08:02.914 --> 00:08:06.351
-You narrate a new docuseries
called "Equal,"

00:08:06.351 --> 00:08:07.786
which is on HBO Max,

00:08:07.786 --> 00:08:10.156
which, by the way,
is killing it right now.

00:08:10.156 --> 00:08:11.190
-Yeah.

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:12.525
-Could you set it up
for everybody?

00:08:12.525 --> 00:08:15.961
-Yeah, you know,
I think we as a society

00:08:15.961 --> 00:08:19.131
know a lot about
LGBTQ+ history

00:08:19.131 --> 00:08:24.437
from 1969, which is
the Stonewall uprising, forward.

00:08:24.437 --> 00:08:26.906
What "Equal" does is it
really talks

00:08:26.906 --> 00:08:29.742
about what came before that.

00:08:29.742 --> 00:08:33.245
You know, the history
that came before 1969.

00:08:33.245 --> 00:08:36.748
So probably around the turn
of the century, even as far back

00:08:36.748 --> 00:08:41.386
as like the late 1800s,
up into the Stonewall uprising.

00:08:41.386 --> 00:08:44.690
And I learned a lot about stuff
that I didn't know.

00:08:44.690 --> 00:08:47.959
And they called and asked me
to be the voice.

00:08:47.959 --> 00:08:49.594
So that's what I did.

00:08:49.594 --> 00:08:52.231
It's really exciting,
and it's really, really good.

00:08:52.231 --> 00:08:53.565
Really empowering.

00:08:53.565 --> 00:08:57.636
-You are so talented,
you are fun, you are fearless.

00:08:57.636 --> 00:08:58.904
We love you here.

00:08:58.904 --> 00:09:01.407
I want to show everyone a clip
of "Equal,"

00:09:01.407 --> 00:09:03.775
which premieres
Thursday on HBO Max.

00:09:03.775 --> 00:09:05.377
Take a look at this.

00:09:05.377 --> 00:09:08.814
-100 years ago, lesbians
and gays could find their fun

00:09:08.814 --> 00:09:11.783
together
in the underground world.

00:09:11.783 --> 00:09:13.352
We're talking
the Roaring Twenties

00:09:13.352 --> 00:09:15.488
and the Dirty Thirties.

00:09:15.488 --> 00:09:21.227
You know, Prohibition,
speakeasies, and the like.

00:09:21.227 --> 00:09:25.330
It was still on the down-low,
but you could find the gay life,

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:28.167
if you knew
where to look for it.

00:09:28.167 --> 00:09:32.504
But by the 1950s,
queer love was forbidden love.

00:09:32.504 --> 00:09:37.176
A conservative chill set in
across postwar America.

00:09:37.176 --> 00:09:39.912
-Billy Porter.
All four episodes of "Equal"

00:09:39.912 --> 00:09:43.382
begin streaming
this Thursday on HBO Max.

00:09:43.382 --> 00:09:46.118
Next time you come on, Billy,
I need that video.

00:09:46.118 --> 00:09:48.086
I'm gonna find it.
I want to hear that.

00:09:48.086 --> 00:09:49.221
-We'll find it.

00:09:49.221 --> 00:09:51.089
I'm sure I will hear
from some folks.

00:09:51.089 --> 00:09:53.225
We got that one, and we got
"Guys and Dolls"

00:09:53.225 --> 00:09:55.327
from when I was
in high school, too.

00:09:55.327 --> 00:09:56.962
They're out there somewhere.
I've seen them.

00:09:56.962 --> 00:09:58.965
-I love that the kids
were waiting for you.

00:09:58.965 --> 00:10:00.332
They were waiting for
your entrance.

00:10:00.332 --> 00:10:02.634
-The children were waiting
for me, honey.

00:10:02.634 --> 00:10:04.236
Gave me applause, darling.

